    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "14",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:14"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "14",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.14",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.14"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The people say to me, “Where are those threats the ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " made against us? Let him carry them out now!”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.15"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "15",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:15"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "15",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.15",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.15"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "16",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:16"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "16",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", I never urged you to bring disaster on them;",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "f",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17.16",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "Probable text",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "bring disaster on them",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "; Hebrew",
              "type": "text"
            },
            {
              "text": "from being a shepherd after you.",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " I did not wish a time of trouble for them. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ", you know this; you know what I have said. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.16",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.16"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "17",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:17"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "17",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Do not be a terror to me; you are my place of safety when trouble comes. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.17",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.17"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Bring disgrace on those who persecute me, but spare me, ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": ". Fill them with terror, but do not terrify me. Bring disaster on them and break them to pieces.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.18"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "18",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:18"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "18",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.18",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.18"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "19",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:19"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "19",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "The ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "text": " said to me, “Jeremiah, go and announce my message at the People's Gate, through which the kings of Judah enter and leave the city; then go to all the other gates of Jerusalem. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.19",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.19"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "20",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:20"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "20",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Tell the kings and all the people of Judah and everyone who lives in Jerusalem and enters these gates, to listen to what I say. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.20",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.20"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "21",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:21"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "21",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "NEH.13.15+NEH.13.16+NEH.13.17+NEH.13.18+NEH.13.19+NEH.13.20+NEH.13.21+NEH.13.22"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Neh 13.15–22",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Tell them that if they love their lives, they must not carry any load on the Sabbath; they must not carry anything in through the gates of Jerusalem ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.21",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.21"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "22",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:22"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "22",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "name": "note",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "style": "x",
            "caller": "#"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "EXO.20.8+EXO.20.9+EXO.20.10"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Ex 20.8–10",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "name": "ref",
              "type": "tag",
              "attrs": {
                "loc": "DEU.5.12+DEU.5.13+DEU.5.14"
              },
              "items": [
                {
                  "text": "Deut 5.12–14",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "or carry anything out of their houses on the Sabbath. They must not work on the Sabbath; they must observe it as a sacred day, as I commanded their ancestors. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.22",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.22"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Their ancestors did not listen to me or pay any attention. Instead, they became stubborn; they would not obey me or learn from me.",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.23"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "para",
      "type": "tag",
      "attrs": {
        "style": "p"
      },
      "items": [
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "23",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:23"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "23",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": " ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.23",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.23"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "24",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:24"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "24",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "“Tell these people that they must obey all my commands. They must not carry any load in through the gates of this city on the Sabbath. They must observe the Sabbath as a sacred day and must not do any work at all. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.24",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.24"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "25",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:25"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "25",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Then their kings and princes will enter the gates of Jerusalem and have the same royal power that David had. Together with the people of Judah and of Jerusalem, they will ride in chariots and on horses, and the city of Jerusalem will always be filled with people. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.25",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.25"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "26",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:26"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "26",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "People will come from the towns of Judah and from the villages round Jerusalem; they will come from the territory of Benjamin, from the foothills, from the mountains, and from southern Judah. They will bring to my Temple burnt offerings and sacrifices, grain offerings and incense, as well as thank-offerings. ",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.26",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.26"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "verse",
          "type": "tag",
          "attrs": {
            "number": "27",
            "style": "v",
            "sid": "JER 17:27"
          },
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "27",
              "type": "text"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "But they must obey me and observe the Sabbath as a sacred day. They must not carry any load through the gates of Jerusalem on that day, for if they do, I will set the gates of Jerusalem on fire. Fire will burn down the palaces of Jerusalem, and no one will be able to put it out.”",
          "type": "text",
          "attrs": {
            "verseId": "JER.17.27",
            "verseOrgIds": [
              "JER.17.27"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
